---------------------------------------------------------------------------
THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS
---------------------------------------------------------------------------

The published application has NO third-party runtime components. It loads no
library, no framework and no font from any origin but its own: every module in
site/app/ is first-party.

On typefaces. The stylesheet names -apple-system, Segoe UI and system-ui. Those
typefaces are indeed under copyright, and this software neither contains nor
distributes any of them. Naming a font family in CSS asks the reader's own
device to use a font it already holds under its own licence; no copy is made
and nothing is redistributed, so no font licence attaches to this software.
Embedding a font file would be the act that created such an obligation, and no
font file is embedded.

The following are build-time tools only. They run on a maintainer's machine to
generate assets, and no part of them is bundled into or redistributed with the
published site:

  Pillow          HPND License          image generation (scripts/build_banner.py,
                                        assets/icon_plate_and_parcel.py)
  python-docx     MIT License           reads the source shopping document
                                        (scripts/extract.py)

The wordmark and icon artwork are first-party. The pixel lettering is drawn
geometrically by assets/banner_plate_and_parcel.py rather than set in a
typeface, so no font is embedded and no font licence attaches to it.

Google Firebase Realtime Database is used as a hosted service, reached over its
public REST and SSE endpoints. No Firebase SDK or other Google code is included
in this software; use of the service is governed by the agreement between the
copyright holder and Google, not by this licence.
